# UI design

Each app has a distinct, high-fidelity look (hospitality operations vs customer vs admin). Do not ship default Material boilerplate, Roboto-only type, or purple-on-white clichés.

## Rules

- New screens use `core/theme` and `core/widgets` first; extract a reusable widget after the second copy
- Honor RTL for Arabic; layouts must not clip or reverse incorrectly
- Dense, scannable ops UI in `managment` (kitchen, POS, tables)
- Inviting customer UI in `sip_sync_flutter`
- Clear, information-dense admin UI in `backoffice`
- Loading, empty, error, and permission-denied states are required
- Micro-interactions on primary actions; keep motion consistent

If the app already has a theme, **extend it**. Only invent a visual language when the app has none yet (see `serverpod-flutter-frontend` skill).
